//! flags: -p ssa

// A callee that branches on a flag its caller was specialized on, in a gang.
//
// `render.specialize(lit)` copies the pixel loop once per value of the flag,
// and each copy calls `shade` with a constant. The vectorizer used to make
// ONE gang variant of `shade` for both copies, keyed only by which arguments
// vary, so the flag stayed a parameter inside it: its branch was linearized
// and both arms ran under a mask in every copy, and a call the flag guarded
// -- a foreign function the gang cannot widen -- was reached from the copy
// that could never make it. Now a constant that the callee's control depends
// on is part of the variant's key (SSA/Vectorize.cpp, parameter_steers_
// control): each copy gets a clone of its own with the constant folded in
// before the clone is vectorized, and the arm no caller of that clone can
// reach is gone. Folded, each clone is one straight line, which the gang
// inlines (inline_pure_variants). What to read for in the golden: no
// variant of `shade` and no call to it; the `lit` copy's loop body a
// multiply by a broadcast 2, the other copy's a load and a store, neither
// with a select or a mask.
func shade(x : f32, lit : bool) -> f32 {
    if lit {
        return x * 2.0;
    }
    return x;
}

func [[export]] render(inp : array[f32, 8], out : mut array[f32, 8],
                       lit : bool) -> void {
    parfor i in 0:8 {
        out[i] = shade(inp[i], lit);
    }
    return;
}

schedule {
    render.specialize(lit);
    render.vectorize(i);
}
